The cat&#x2019;s out of the bag.

Amanda Seyfried not only appears in Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim&#x2019;s Elizabeth Holmes documentary &#x201C; You Can See Everything ,&#x201D; but her winning turn as Holmes (and herself) may make history as the first doc performance to win an acting Oscar (and perhaps the first to win an Oscar and an Emmy for playing the same person, since Seyfried previously depicted Holmes in Hulu&#x2019;s &#x201C; The Dropout ?&#x201D;) Distributor A24 kept Seyfried&#x2019;s participation in the film a secret so as not to spoil the surprise &#x2014; demanding press outlets not mention it in their reviews &#x2014; and the &#x201C;Mean Girls&#x201D; actress lends a layer of candor and relatability to the otherwise odd and opaque proceedings. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Ben Affleck Raved About Robert Pattinson’s ‘The Odyssey’ Performance, Recalls Matt Damon: He Said ‘It Was Like Watching a Guy Run Into an Avalanche’ Anne Hathaway to Receive American Riviera Award at Santa Barbara International Film Festival

Now that the film is a bona fide cultural phenomenon, becoming the first documentary in decades to cross $100 million at the global box office , pushing the boundaries of the genre, inspiring countless memes and cementing Seyfried&#x2019;s status as an awards contender, she&#x2019;s been making the press rounds. Her latest stop was Jimmy Fallon&#x2019;s &#x201C;Tonight Show&#x201D; Tuesday evening.

&#x201C;At first, they had just done their whole documentary and then I just jumped in kind of at the last-minute, and it turned into something else,&#x201D; Seyfried told Fallon.

Once Holmes is sent away to prison, Fielder tapped Seyfried to take her place, with the actress reenacting scenes as Holmes. Seyfried told the host that she had a wealth of research at her fingertips to draw from since Holmes was a &#x201C;very public-facing person,&#x201D; but the &#x201C;only footage I had of her in the present-day, or at that point when they were living with her, is the documentary itself, and I couldn&#x2019;t watch the footage until I got to set.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Seyfried alluded to the &#x201C;You Can See Everything&#x201D; script being kept under lock and key, revealing, &#x201C;I didn&#x2019;t know what the script would be until I got to set, or it would be, like, five-factor authentication app where I could maybe read it the night before.&#x201D;

EXCLUSIVE: Ahead of the finale of hit K-drama The Remarried Empress , Korean actress Shin Mina , who plays Empress Navier in the show, talked to Deadline about her experiences of playing the role and shared her thoughts on why the show is such a huge success.

She also shared some tips on what viewers could look out for in the final two episodes, which are dropping on Disney+ and Hulu later today (November 25).

Also starring Ju Jihoon , Lee Jongsuk and Lee Seyoung, The Remarried Empress has been a breakout hit in Korea and internationally, becoming the most viewed local original premiere of all time on Disney+ globally, just three days after its launch on November 3. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Black Friday Streaming Deals Offered By Disney+, HBO Max, Paramount+, Peacock & More Casting Kelly Rowland Joins Hulu's 'Reasonable Doubt' For Season 5

Premiere views increased worldwide around 40% between its first and second weeks of streaming, with Latin America leading as the fastest-growing region, with views increasing by 43%, followed by APAC and EMEA at 39% and the U.S. at 37%. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Based on a Naver webtoon , the story revolves around Empress Navier and her dignified response when her husband, Emperor Sovieshu of the Eastern Kingdom, takes a slave girl as a concubine and suggests marrying her. While keeping her composure, Navier becomes closer to Crown Prince Heinrey, who can take the form of a magical bird. At the end of episode eight, we saw Navier inform her husband that would she accompany the Prince to the Western Kingdom to attend his coronation as king following his father&#x2019;s death.

This was Shin&#x2019;s first time playing an Empress in a romantasy epic, although she found some common ground with characters she&#x2019;s played before: &#x201C;I&#x2019;ve appeared in a period drama before, Arang And The Magistrate , a fantasy-infused historical series, but I played a ghost in that one, so it was a very different experience from a traditional historical drama,&#x201D; she tells Deadline.

&#x201C;This time, even though the setting is an imaginary era, playing a character with a symbolic status in a world with social classes felt new to me. Above all, I loved that Navier&#x2019;s dignity, strength, and wisdom are at the heart of the story. And I thought she was an incredibly proactive and appealing character, since in the end she chooses to remarry on her own terms.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Shin admits she also got a kick out of wearing so many different styles of dresses. While Korean period dramas are usually filmed in traditional Hanbok, The Remarried Empress uses European-style costumes and sets and was filmed in castles and palaces in Germany and the Czech Republic.

&#x201C;I wore so many dresses and tried so many different hairstyles. I kept thinking, &#x2018;when will I ever get to film in dresses this gorgeous again?&#x2019; so I enjoyed every moment while acting. Of course, the costumes weren&#x2019;t always comfortable,&#x201D; Shin laughs.

But while she plays an Empress in a fantasy setting in the series, Shin says Navier is not so different to characters she&#x2019;s played before: "There are seeds of love in Navier&#x2019;s heart, too. As they slowly sprout, she realizes how she truly feels and chooses a new love. I think those emotional shifts, and the moments of facing love, connect with the characters in other romance projects I&#x2019;ve played."

On the huge success of the show, Shin says the popularity of the original webtoon meant that audiences around the world were looking forward to the adaptation, but that also put a lot of pressure on the cast and crew. &#x201C;We knew many people were looking forward to the drama, but I&#x2019;m sure some were also worried about a live-action adaptation,&#x201D; Shin says. &#x201C;So I was really curious how this new challenge would be received.

&#x201C;When we started filming, I was worried about whether I could quickly immerse myself in this unfamiliar setting. But after shooting a few episodes, those concerns disappeared naturally. At some point, I was completely focused on the story unfolding within that world.

&#x201C;Just as the cast did, viewers got immersed in this world and its characters faster than I expected, which was surprising and made me very grateful. I never imagined the drama would be loved this much.&#x201D;

She says that, in particular, fans are cheering on the character of Empress Navier. &#x201C;I think people relate to the situation Navier is in. She may look strong and cold on the outside, but she cares deeply for her people and shows warmth toward the imperial maids and Queen. I&#x2019;m grateful that viewers understand and empathize not only with her human side, but also with the responsibility of living as the perfect empress and the pressure that comes with it.&#x201D;

Shin adds that she enjoyed filming in Europe, and that shooting in real castles helped her get into character: &#x201C;Being able to film in places steeped in another country&#x2019;s culture and history felt very new to me. Wearing gorgeous dresses and filming in such exotic locations actually helped me become even more immersed in the world of the series.&#x201D;

As for tonight&#x2019;s finale, Shin doesn&#x2019;t want to drop any spoilers, but has this to say: &#x201C;I hope viewers will watch the finale wondering what the Eastern Empire will look like without Empress Navier. I also hope you&#x2019;ll cheer on Navier&#x2019;s future after making a new choice, the future of the Western Kingdom, and the future she will build together with Heinrey.

&#x201C;Navier has always lived with genuine care for the Eastern Empire and its people. So I&#x2019;d love for viewers to pay attention to what she feels as she leaves her homeland and chooses a new life, and to the emotions of someone standing at the start of a new beginning.&#x201D;

In addition to Arang And The Magistrat e, Shin&#x2019;s previous credits also include My Girlfriend Is A Gumiho (2010), Oh My Venus (2015), Hometown Cha-Cha-Cha (2021), Our Blues (2022) and No Gain No Love (2024). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-articleX","mid-article","btf","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() ; });

Produced by Studio N, The Remarried Empress is directed by Cho Suwon and adapted for screen by Yeoh Geena and Hyun Choongyeol. Ju Jihoon plays Emperor Sovieshu, with Lee Jongsuk playing Crown Prince Heinrey and Lee Seyoung as the slave girl Rashta.

We first got a glimpse of how big the show would become at this year&#x2019;s Busan International Film Festival, which premiered the first three episodes to packed theaters. So far the producers are keeping mum on whether there will be a second season, but that looks like something the fans are hoping for.

The final two episodes are dropping today at 5:00pm KST, 4:00pm HKT, 8:00am GMT and midnight PST.

Jenna Ushkowitz, who starred as Tina Cohen-Chang for the entirety of &#x201C; Glee ,&#x201D; is reflecting on how the Fox series addressed the real-life death of her fellow cast member Cory Monteith, and why she now feels it &#x201C;wasn&#x2019;t the right thing&#x201D; to do at the time.

Monteith played Finn Hudson, the show&#x2019;s leading man and quarterback-turned-Glee club member, until he died of an accidental overdose in July 2013. The show honored the actor with a Season 5 episode titled &#x201C;The Quarterback&#x201D; that October, a tribute to Monteith that also explained Hudson&#x2019;s passing within the context of the show. (The episode makes no mention of how Hudson died.) blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories How to Watch Billy Evans' First TV Interview About 'You Can See Everything' Online Disney Inks Deal With Creator Zach King for 'Illusion Shorts' Inspired by Mouse House's Movies and Experiences

&#x201C;To shoot [the tribute episode] &#x2018;The Quarterback&#x2019;&#x2026; I think it wasn&#x2019;t the right thing,&#x201D; Ushkowitz said on the &#x201C;We Need to Talk &#x201D; podcast Monday. &#x201C;And I think everybody collectively agrees that it&#x2019;s maybe not the thing that we should have done, because we were grieving both privately and publicly.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I think the fans definitely needed something, because they loved Cory so dearly like we did, and [loved] Finn so dearly,&#x201D; she said. &#x201C;But it&#x2019;s a really hard thing to be grieving your friend and be a character grieving their friend at the same time.&#x201D;

&#x201C;It was like, too soon for that. [It] was not fun, [I] don&#x2019;t want to remember that time,&#x201D; she continued. &#x201C;The show itself was never the same. He was the heart of the show, our friend, most importantly, and our leader. He really was the quarterback for us. He held everybody together. He hosted parties for the crew. He was the kindest. He knew everybody&#x2019;s names. He just was such a good person, a kind person.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Ushkowitz also noted that the &#x201C;nobody&#x201D; on the show &#x201C;had the tools to deal with&#x201D; Monteith&#x2019;s death. &#x201C;Even our creators, they were dealing with grief too. So nobody had the tools.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Glee&#x201D; first premiered in Sept. 2009, and in addition to Monteith and Ushkowitz, starred Lea Michele, Naya Rivera, Dianna Agron , Matthew Morrison, Jane Lynch, Heather Morris, Chris Colfer and more. A reboot of the show was set at Disney+ and Hulu in October.

Speaking with Variety earlier this month, co-creator Ian Brennan said he&#x2019;s &#x201C;really excited about it.&#x201D; &#x201C;It&#x2019;s going to be a lot of fun,&#x201D; he added. &#x201C;We&#x2019;re still figuring a lot of it out,&#x201D; Brennan said on addressing the deaths of Monteith and Rivera, who died in 2020. &#x201C;That&#x2019;s going to be part of it, that sadness and that loss. But still in all, I think [&#x201C;Glee&#x201D;] is too big of a thing to sort of let lay. There&#x2019;s something about that feels right right now.&#x201D;

Heavy hangs the head that wears the crown &#x2014; or in this case, the samurai topknot &#x2014; in Kiyoshi Kurosawa 's absorbing, clean-lined literary adaptation " The Samurai and the Prisoner ," for which the veteran filmmaker brings to life a storied period of swirling discontent in Japanese history with such evocative restraint that it becomes distinctly modern. And yet this is no work of genre deconstruction, and there's little of Kurosawa's familiar, eerie experimentation with narrative form. Instead, "Samurai" is classical, if pared-back, in approach &#x2014; at once a satisfyingly linked series of rousing whodunnits, a tricksy game of mental cat-and-mouse and a trenchant, often rather moving, exploration of the nature of true leadership, in all its solitude and sacrifice.&#xA0; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories How Netflix and the NFL Hope to Establish New Thanksgiving Eve Tradition With Game and U2 Half-Time Show: ‘We Want to Create Those Global Water Cooler Moments’ Shannon Elizabeth to Star in and Produce Psychological Thriller ‘SweatBox’ (EXCLUSIVE)

The leader here is Araki Murashige ( Masahiro Motoki , excelling in portraying the character's conflicted charisma) the lord of Arioka Castle during the Azuchi era at the end of the 16th century. As our story begins, the formerly loyal Murashige is in rebellion against powerful regional magnate Oda Nobunaga, citing Nobunaga's cruelty, ruthlessness and thirst for power as his reasons. In response, Nobunaga and his local allies have sent forces to besiege the castle, which has become a fortress. Within its geometric courtyards and spartan, tatami-matted interiors, Murashige paces and plots his next move, consulting with the leaders of the clans under his control and being occasionally comforted by his devout wife Chiyoho (Yuriko Yoshitaka), whose enmity toward Nobunaga may outmatch even that of her husband.&#xA0; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

As a last-ditch attempt at a diplomatic resolution, Oda Nobunaga sends an envoy to Arioka Castle. Kuroda Kanbei ( Masaki Suda , reuniting with Kurosawa after the 2024 thriller "Cloud") is a samurai famous for his intelligence and political cunning, but his arguments as to why Murashige should return to the Nobunaga fold fall on deaf ears. Kanbei, rebuffed and prevented from leaving, expects to be put to death, according to the samurai code, by which messages are sent and justice dispensed at the tip of a sword.

Instead, Murashige orders him imprisoned in the castle's dungeon, a move that is part clemency, chiming with his recent adoption of a more progressive, and very un -samurai,&#xA0;attitude toward the value of human life ("Do not die for me," he will later order one of his retainers), but also part strategy. Murashige knows that when word that Kanbei lives on gets back to Nobunaga, the rival lord will assume it can only be because Kanbei switched sides, which will be a useful propaganda coup. Almost all of the decisions Murashige makes are similarly double-edged, like the dagger wears he tucked into the sash of his kimono.&#xA0;&#xA0;&#xA0;

But then news arrives that one of the lords whose support Murashige was relying on has strayed over to Nobunaga's side, which presents another dilemma. As was customary in feudal times, the defector's young son was living with Murashige as a hostage/honored guest, and now that his father has abandoned his patron, the penalty ought to be the child's death. But quailing at the prospect of killing an eight-year-old boy (and one to whom the childless Chiyoho has become quite attached), however much the boy himself begs to thus atone for his father's betrayal, instead Murashige orders him spared and protected.

So imagine his feelings of impotence and rage when the boy is killed anyway, by an impossible arrow that finds its target through a tiny crack in a door and then, apparently, vanishes. Is this some kind of supernatural payback for Murashige's rejection of centuries of samurai tradition, or is there a rational explanation? Unable to make sense of the crime, eventually Murashige decides to consult the clever Kanbei, who is bored down there in the dungeon alone, and grateful for the intellectual distraction of solving this puzzle. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

It is winter when all this occurs, but before the year is out, there will be three more mysteries, each corresponding to a successive season. In spring, an enemy's decapitated head, brought back as proof of a successful battle, goes missing. In summer, someone purloins Murashige's favorite ceramic tea-kettle, which he had intended to give as a valuable gift to seal an alliance. And in autumn, a stray bolt of lightning kills a member of the entourage at the exact moment he's about to reveal an important secret. Each of these enigmatic incidents carries the whiff of divine retribution, which in each case the anti-superstition and non-devout Murashige will seek Kanebi's help to debunk.

This four-chapter structure and the contained castle, with its rooms and courtyards so stripped-down as to appear abstract, can give the whole enterprise the feel of a TV show or miniseries. But in an age when Japan-set period TV literary adaptations have reached the level of sophistication of 2024's "Shogun," for example, that is not necessarily a bad thing. DP Yasuyuki Sasaki's camerawork is stylish and sure and occasionally striking, as in the dungeon lit by shafts of light that slice through the cracks in the walls like laser beams. And Koichi Takahashi's editing keeps things ebbing and flowing within each single section, but also finds ways for each to build on and enlarge the one that came before.

But mostly the watchword in the craft design is simplicity, like Kurosawa is preparing a magic trick and showing us, look! No hidden accomplices or secret trapdoors! And it helps to have an uncluttered stage, when the plot is so baroque and the (routinely excellent) cast of clan chiefs and nobles and advisers and trusty retainers is so numerous. Don't worry, they get fewer all the time: Fans of Genki Kawamura's "Exit 8," for example, will be happy to see Kochi Yamato, after his breakout as the creepily smiling Walking Man in the 2025 videogame adaptation, but they are also fairly warned not to get too attached to him.

The same could be said for roughly half the populous but well-differentiated&#xA0;cast. As the seasons pass, the castle ranks are thinned by defection or death, and increasingly it feels like Murashige's only real friend is the enemy he threw in prison a year ago. Kanbei is locked up but in many ways freer than a weighed-down Murashige, with his proscribed roles and responsibilities, and his conflicted loyalty to a code he no longer believes in. Kurosawa's highly entertaining adaptation knows that just because you are chained does not make you a prisoner, any more than having wealth and power can reliably make you free.

Sighle Williams served customers at a Florida burger joint for 37 years. And on her last day at Mac&#x2019;s Drive Thru, it seemed like the entire city of Gainesville came out to say goodbye.

&#x201C;A lot of people told me they were going to come. But I wasn&#x2019;t expecting that many people,&#x201D; Williams tells Variety . Mac&#x2019;s had a three-hour line of cars during her final shift. The restaurant was so busy they actually ran out of burgers. &#x201C;Some of the people that showed up that day didn&#x2019;t even know me,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s a good feeling that I made a difference in a lot of people&#x2019;s lives.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Chris Colfer Says 'Glee' Reboot 'Conversations' About Kurt's Return Are Ongoing: 'From What I Heard, It Sounded Very Funny and Like a Good Idea' Jane Lynch Wants to Return for 'Glee' Reboot: 'I Would Love to Do Sue Sylvester for the Rest of My Life'

Williams is the subject of &#x201C; One Last Order ,&#x201D; a 20-minute documentary that hit Netflix on Tuesday. The film, co-directed by the restaurant owner&#x2019;s daughter, follows Williams as she hugs emotional customers and recounts spending half her life behind the drive-thru window.

Williams says the cameras didn&#x2019;t faze her, but she got emotional during &#x201C;a moment when I sat in my car and realized it was my last day of work, and how all the people came out to see me off. It was awesome.&#x201D;

&#x201C;It was overwhelming as well,&#x201D; Williams adds. &#x201C;I was so hyped up, I didn&#x2019;t eat all day. I didn&#x2019;t even go to the restroom.&#x201D;

Mac&#x2019;s made three times its normal sales on Williams&#x2019; last day. As a retirement gift, the owners gave her every dollar that passed through the fast-food window. Between the day&#x2019;s earnings and generous tips, Williams made nearly an entire year&#x2019;s salary in a single day, according to the documentary. Williams tells Variety the gift has allowed her to &#x201C;catch up on some things and save for a rainy day.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Since retiring, Williams has been back at Mac&#x2019;s a handful of times &#x2014; mostly to catch up with her friends. &#x201C;I miss working, yes, but I also miss the community,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;I miss the customers. That is what I mainly miss.&#x201D;

Williams became a beloved fixture in Gainesville for her sunny demeanor and her unique ability to memorize repeat customers&#x2019; orders. One customer in the documentary says seeing Williams in the drive-thru window is &#x201C;like seeing a rainbow every day.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Everybody has their own things going on in their life, and sometimes you just have to take a moment to say, &#x2018;Hey, how are you doing?&#x2019; They could be having a rough day, and it made a difference,&#x201D; Williams says. &#x201C;Sometimes you have a car full of kids and the mama trying to get the order right. Some people come and they don&#x2019;t really know what they want. You just have to be patient. People appreciate that.&#x201D;

Williams worked for 37 years while raising five girls on her own. When her sister struggled with drug addiction, she stepped up to parent her two daughters. And a few years later, she took in her niece&#x2019;s three kids.

Asked how she remained so cheerful despite difficult circumstances, Williams says, &#x201C;I&#x2019;m just a positive person, I guess. They had to go to school. I had to go to work. I had to make sure we had the lights on, doctor&#x2019;s appointments and everything. I can&#x2019;t explain it.&#x201D;

When Netflix posted the trailer for the film in early November, it went viral on X, gaining more than 11 million views. Williams, who has accompanied the documentary at seven or eight festivals, says she felt like a celebrity before the film even premiered. The week it launched on Netflix, Williams appeared on &#x201C;CBS Mornings&#x201D; and &#x201C;The Jennifer Hudson Show.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I&#x2019;ve been practicing for the Spirit Tunnel,&#x201D; she says of the talk show&#x2019;s viral entrance videos. &#x201C;I can dance a little bit. I&#x2019;m going to be cool with it and rock with it.&#x201D;
